hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4174","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Thawr told me Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Khaled Ibn Ma’dan, on the authority of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they said: O Messenger of God, tell us about Yourself, and he said: “The call of my father Abraham, and the good news of Jesus, and when my mother saw when she was pregnant with me that a light had come out of her, illuminating my eyes and his. From the land of the Levant.” Al-Hakim said: “Khaled bin Ma’dan is one of the best of the Tabi’een. He accompanied Muadh bin Jabal and those of the Companions after him. If he narrated a hadith to the Companions, for it has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4174 - True"
"4175","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, he said: I said to Abi Al-Yaman: Abu Bakr bin Abi told you. Maryam Al-Ghassani, on the authority of Saeed bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I am with God at the beginning of The Book is the Seal of the Prophets, and Adam was one with mud in his clay, and I will inform you of the interpretation of that, the call of my father Abraham and the good news of Jesus to his people. And my mother saw a vision that a light came out of her, illuminating the palaces of the Levant. He said: Yes. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration that bears witness to the hadith. “The first”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4175 - True"
"4176","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Baghdadi told us, Hashim bin Marthad Al-Tabarani told us, Yaqoub bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri told us, about Abdul Aziz bin Imran, Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhrama, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, He said: “Abdul-Muttalib said: We came to Yemen during the winter journey and camped on a Jewish rabbi, and a man from the people of the Zabur said to me: O Abdul Request: Do you permit me to look at your body as long as it is not private? He said: He opened one of my nostrils and looked into it, then looked into the other and said: I bear witness that in one of your hands is kingdom and in the other is prophecy. I see this in Bani Zahra, so how is that? I said: I don’t know. He said: Do you have any rumors? He said: I said: What is the rumor? He said: A wife. I said: As for today, no. He said: If you come, marry one of them. Abdul-Muttalib returned to Mecca and married Hala, the daughter of Wahb bin Abdul Manaf bore him Hamzah and Safiyya, and Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib married Amina bint Wahb and she gave birth to Rasul May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Quraysh said, “When Abdullah married Aminah, ‘Abdullah prevailed upon his father.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4176 - Ya’qub and his sheikh are weak"
"4177","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Farisi told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Kinani told us, my father told me, On the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa was narrating on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with them both, she said: “He was a Jew who He lived in Mecca and traded there, and when it was the night in which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born, he said in a gathering of Quraysh: O people! Quraysh, was there a baby born among you tonight? They said: By God, we do not know him. He said: God is great. But if he makes you a mistake, there is no problem, so watch and memorize what I am telling you. This was born. Tonight, the Prophet of this last nation has a mark between his shoulders containing intermittent hairs as if they were the mane of a horse. He will not breastfeed for two nights, and that is A demon from the jinn put his two fingers into his mouth and prevented him from breastfeeding. The people left their seat astonished at his statement. And his hadith: When they reached their homes, each of them informed his family, and they said: A boy has been born to Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib. They called him Muhammad, so the people met and said: Did you hear the Jew’s speech? Have you heard of the birth of this boy? So they set off until they came to the Jew. So they told him the news. He said: So go with me until I look at him. So they went out and brought him to safety. He said: Bring out your son to us. So she took him out, and they revealed his back to him, and he saw that mole, and the Jew fell unconscious, and when he recovered, they said: Woe to you, what is the matter with you? He said: By God, the prophecy from the Children of Israel has disappeared. You rejoiced in it, O people of Quraysh. By God, they will exert power over you. He will emerge. He heard about it from the east and the west, and among the group that day were those to whom the Jew said: What Hisham bin Al-Walid bin Al-Mughirah said? Musafer bin Abi Amr, Ubaidah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul Muttalib, and Utbah bin Rabi’ah, a young man above puberty, among a group of Banu Manaf. And others from the Quraysh said: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. There have been reports that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born He was circumcised, pleased, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born in the house in the alley known as Al-Mudkal Alley in Mecca, and I prayed in it, which is the house Which was after the migration of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the hands of Aqeel bin Abi Talib and in the hands of his son after him.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4177 - Following Al-Hakim’s correction of the hadith, not denying its authenticity"
"4178","As Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Ali bin Al-Hussein told me that Amr bin Othman told him on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, that he said: O Messenger of God, will you descend in Did you live in Mecca? He said: “Did Aqeel leave for us a quarter or a dur?” Aqeel was the inheritor of Abu Talib, but neither Ali nor Ja’far inherited from him because they were Muslims: “The two sheikhs used this hadith as evidence.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4178 - They took it out"
"4179","Abu Amr bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, and Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us in Nishapur, saying: Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd told us. Al-Wahhab bin Ata’, Saeed reported, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ghailan bin Jarir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ma’bad al-Zamani, on the authority of Abu Qatada Al-Ansari said that a Bedouin asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about fasting on Monday. He said: “That is the day on which I was born and the Messenger of God was revealed.” Ali in it.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Rather, Muslim used as evidence the hadith of Shu’bah on the authority of Qatada with this chain of transmission: Fasting on the day of Arafat expiates the Sunnah and what came before it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4179 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4180","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born in the year of the Elephant.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4180 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4181","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Ahmasi told us in Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid bin Al-Rabi’ told us, my father told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born “The Day of the Elephant.” Humayd ibn al-Rabi’ was the only one to use this word in this hadith, and he was not followed up on it."
"4182","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Shabawayh, the chief of Marwa, told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Naysaburi told us, Ali bin Mahran told us, Salama bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was born twelve nights ago in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal.”"
"4183","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Muttalib told me Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qais Ibn Makhramah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Ibn Makhramah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I were born in the year An elephant is like two female lions.” Ibn Ishaq said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was twenty years old in the year of ‘Ukaz.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. Muslim, and they did not produce it.”"
"4184","Abu Ja`far al-Baghdadi told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Amr bin Aoun al-Wasiti told us, Khalid bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al Abbas bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Kandir bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, who said: I performed Hajj in pre-Islamic times, and suddenly I saw a man circling At home, he was shaking and saying:\n [The sea of rage]\n\n My Lord, return to me my rider Muhammad...return him to me and appear with me as a hand\n So I said: Who is this? They said: Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim sent his son Muhammad’s son in search of camels for him, and he did not send him for any need unless he succeeded in it, and he succeeded in it. He took it slow, and it was not long before Muhammad and the camels came and embraced him and said: O my son, I am upset over you as I have never been upset over anything. By God, I will never send you for any need, and you will never leave me after this.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it, and it was agreed upon. The two Sheikhs are from the names of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after Muhammad, Ahmad, Al-Hashir, Al-Aqib, and Al-Mahi.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4184 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4185","So Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Hatim Al-Muzaki told us about Marwa, Abdullah bin Hatim told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Musa, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named for us names, some of which we have memorized and some of which We have not forgotten that he said: “I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and al-Muqaffa, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of Repentance and the Battle.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4185 - True"
"4186","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hasan bin Humaid told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abu Wahshiyah, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I am Muhammad and Ahmad “By the rhyme, the gatherer, the seal, and the end.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4186 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4187","Professor Abu Al-Walid and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Al-Layth bin told us. Saad, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am Abu Al-Qasim “God gives and I swear.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4187 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4188","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Abdul-Wahid bin Sharik told us, and Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Malhan told us, they said: Amr bin Khaled told us. Al-Harrani, told us Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, and Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, who said: “When Abraham, the son of the Prophet, was born, he prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Gabriel came to him and said: “Peace be upon you, O father of Abraham.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4188 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4189","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told me, in Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Ubaid bin Ishaq al-Attar told us, al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, my father told me, my father told me, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ascended He greeted God on the pulpit, thanked God and praised Him, then said: “Who am I?” We said: The Messenger of God. He said: “Yes, but who am I?” We said: You are Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib bin Hashim bin Abd Manaf. He said: “I am the master of the children of Adam, and I am not proud.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4189 - No, by God, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel is abandoned and damaged."
"4190","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Affan told us, Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, Asim bin Kulayb told us, on the authority of his father, He said: The stepdaughter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Zainab, may God be pleased with her, spoke to me, and I said to her: Tell me about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who was he? How harmful was it? She said: “And from whomever it was except from Mudar from the son of an-Nadr ibn Kinanah.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4190 - True"
"4191","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Muzaki and Muhammad bin Yaqoub al-Hafiz told me, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Thaqafi told us, Abu Yahya told us, Sadaqah told us. Ibn Sabiq, he said: I read from Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, he said: Mutalib Ibn Abdullah Ibn Qais Ibn Makhramah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He mentioned the birth of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “His father died and his mother was pregnant with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim and it was not “He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4191 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4192","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yusuf bin Abdullah Al-Khwarizmi told us, in Bayt al-Maqdis, Abu Sa’id Yahya bin Suleiman told us. Al-Jafifi, Yahya bin Yaman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He visited his mother’s grave in a thousand veils, and he was not seen crying more than that day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Only Muslim narrated the hadith of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father: “I asked my Lord for permission to ask forgiveness for my mother, but He did not He gives me permission.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4192 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4193","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Abdul Wahid told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, he said: I heard Ka’b bin Malik saying: “When I greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said, and he His face shines, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was happy, his face would shine as if it were a piece of the moon, and this was known from him. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and they narrated, but did not narrate, this word.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4193 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4194","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Amr Al-Ahmasi told me about Kufa, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dukin told us, Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Uthman ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr ibn Mut’im, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There was no Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is neither tall nor short, with thick palms and feet, a large head and beard, with a huge reddish complexion. He has long, long legs. When he walks, he leans forward as if he were walking down a cliff. I have never seen anyone like him before or after him, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with these words.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4194 - True"
"4195","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, my father told me, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had the shape of the eyes at the side of the mouth.” I said: What are the shapes of the eyes? He said: “Yadam Hatheem.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it."
"4196","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, On the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not laugh except with a smile, and there would be a lump in his legs,” and whenever I looked To him I said: “I use kohl for the eyes but not with kohl.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4196 - Hajjaj’s hadith is soft"
"4197","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Humaid bin Ibrahim Al-Sayegh told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah said: “I saw the seal of prophethood on the back of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, like a dove’s egg.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4197 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4198","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Hatim al-Kashshi told me, Abd bin Humaid told us, Abu Asim told me, on the authority of Ezra bin Thabit, Alaba told me Ibn Ahmar Al-Yashkuri, on the authority of Abu Zaid, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Abu Zaid, come closer and wipe my back.” He said: So I approached. Then I wiped his back and put my fingers on the ring, then I winked at them, and it was said to him: What is the ring? He said: “His hair is gathered at his shoulders.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4198 - True"
"4199","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told us, and Abu Bakr al-Quta’i told us about others, who said: Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Hammad bin Khalid, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4199 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4200","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zar’ah Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Dimashqi told us, Ali bin Ayyash told us, Hariz bin Uthman told us, I said to Abdullah bin Busr Al-Salami: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Was he an old man? He said: “There were white hairs on his neck.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"4201","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Ruqi told us, Husayn bin Ayyash Al-Ruqi told us, Ja’far bin Burqan told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, saying: Anas bin Malik came to Medina and Omar bin Abdul Aziz, its governor, and Omar sent to him and said To the Messenger: Ask him: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dye his hair? I saw some of his hair being colored, and Anas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to enjoy black hair, and if I had counted it, he would not have come to me.” Of the gray hairs on his head and beard, I would not have more than eleven gray hairs, but rather this one was colored with the perfume that he used to perfume himself with. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, felt: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4201 - True"
"4202","Abu Saeed Al-Ahmasi told me, Al-Hussein bin Humaid told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Samurah said: “There were nothing on the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except white hairs at the parting of his head when he applied the oil and the oil applied them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4202 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4203","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik Ibn Umayr, on the authority of Iyad Ibn Laqit, on the authority of Abu Rimthah, said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wearing two green garments, and he had hair. He has grown gray hair, and his gray hair is red stained with henna.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4203 - True"
"4204","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told me, Muhammad bin Kunasa told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Aisha, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, become young? She said: “God would not like him to be white.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, preserved on the authority of Hisham, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4204 - Sahih Mahfouz"
"4205","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Muslim told us, that Hajjaj bin Minhal told them, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit told us, he said: It was said to Anas: What was the gray hair of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “God has no problem with gray hair if there are only seventeen or eighteen hairs on his head.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not They bring it out, and this word was only known by Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and it is said by a very strange Anas.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4205 - According to Muslim’s condition, which is strange"
"4206","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, Ayyub told us, Humaid bin Muhammad told us. Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burdah, who said: Aisha brought out to us a damp garment and a thick garment and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested in These two “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4206 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4207","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan Al-Sukari told us, Sulayman bin Dawood Al-Manqari told us, Abdullah bin Idris told us, He said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. He said: “It was for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4207 - True"
"4208","It was narrated to us by Ahmad bin Yahya al-Muqri, in Kufa, by Abdullah bin Ghannam, by Ibrahim bin Ishaq al-Ja’fi, by Hibban bin Ali. On the authority of Idris Al-Awdi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a horse called Al-Murtajiz, and his she-camel is Al-Uqsa, his mule is Dalal, his donkey is poor, his armor is strong, and his sword is Dhul-Faqar.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4208 - Hibban bin Ali considered him weak"
"4209","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih narrated to us, and Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, and Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Awqi narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Budail bin Maysara, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Maysara Al Fakhr, he said: I said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: When did I become a prophet? He said: “And Adam is between the soul and the body.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and it is witnessed by the hadith of Al-Awza’i which “”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4209 - True"
"4210","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Sulaiman bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl told us, Muhammad bin Hashim Al-Baalbaki told us, Abu Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When did prophecy become necessary for you? He said: “Between the creation of Adam and the breathing of the spirit into him.”"
"4211","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Bakr told us Muawiyah, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not curse a paper. “For I saw that he had one or two gardens.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, and the purpose in quoting it is “\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4211 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4212","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell me, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told me, Yunus bin Bukayr told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Abdul-Malik bin Abdullah bin Abi Sufyan bin Al-Alaa bin Jariyah Al-Thaqafi, and he was aware. He said: Waraqah bin Nawfal bin Asad said Ibn Abdul-Uzza, while Khadija mentioned to him about the affairs of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: in poetry: «\n [Simple Sea]\n Oh men and the waste of time and destiny... and there is nothing that God has decreed without\n Even Khadija invites me to tell her... and she has no news of the unseen.\n She came to ask me about it so I could tell her...something that I see people will come to in the end.\n So she told me about something that I had heard about...in the past, long ago and in the present era.\n That Ahmad comes to him and Gabriel informs him that you are sent to mankind.\n So I said, “Whatever you hope will be accomplished... God bless you, so hope for the best and wait.”\n And send him to us so that we may ask him about what he sees during sleep and at night.\n When he came to us, he said, “A wondrous area...from which the tops of skin and hair stand out.”\n Indeed, I saw the Trustee of God facing me...in one of the most magnificent images.\n Then it continued and I was terrified by the fear of the trees around me.\n So I said my suspicion, and I do not know whether he believes me... that you will be sent to recite the surah revealed.\n And I will come to you if you announce their call... for jihad without any reproach or difficulty.”"
"4213","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, Jeddi told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Thabit told us. Al-Zuhri, Al-Zubayr bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Huwayrith, on the authority of Qabbath bin Ashim Al-Kinani, then Al-Laythi, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prophesied And he greeted the heads of forty elephants.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it. Rather, Al-Bukhari narrated the hadith of Ikrimah on the authority of Ibn Abbas: He was sent when he was forty years old. The evidence for the authenticity of the hadith of Qabath bin Ashim is the choice of the master of the Successors of this saying: “As Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mil bin Al-Hasan told me, narrated by Al-Bukhari and Muslim. Al-Fadl bin Muhammad narrated to us Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: “It was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was forty-three years old.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4213 - Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Thabit. Wah"
"4214","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, “ On the authority of Khadija, may God be pleased with her, that she said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the revelation, he was greatly alarmed by that. So I said: From what I saw of his distress, your Lord has certainly afflicted you because of what he sees of your distress, so God revealed: {Your Lord has not left you nor has He afflicted you} [Al-Duha: 3] “This is a hadith.” The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not take it out as a chain of transmission in it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4214 - Sahih mursal"
"4215","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Gabriel: “What prevents you from visiting us more often?” Why are you visiting us? So God Almighty revealed {And We do not send down except by the command of your Lord} [Maryam: 64] to His saying: {And your Lord is not forgetful} [Maryam: 64] “This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4215 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4216","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maymun told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Qur’an was separated from the remembrance and placed in the House of Glory in the lowest heaven and made Gabriel, peace be upon him, revealed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. {And We recited it in a chant} [Al-Furqan: 32] Sufyan said: “Five verses and the like.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4216 - True"
"4217","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ziyad the grammarian told us, Ibn Abi Talib told us, Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, my father told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Ayyub, narrating on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Shamasa, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, compiling the Qur’an from pieces of paper.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it contains clear evidence. “The Qur’an was only compiled during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4217 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4218","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Ali bin Hakim told us, Muammar bin Suleiman told us, On the authority of Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him, when Gabriel, peace be upon him, descended and said: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, he knew that it was a surah. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4218 - Following Al-Hakim’s correction of hadith no"
"4219","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d told us, on the authority of Jami` bin Shaddad, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah al-Muharbi, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passing by the market of Dhu al-Majaz and I was in A seller of mine, and he passed by wearing a red robe, and I heard him say: “O people, say there is no god but Allah and you will succeed,” and a man following him shot him. He made his heel bleed with stones, and he said: O people, do not obey this man, for he is a liar. So I said: Who is this? It was said: A boy from Banu Abd al-Muttalib. When God revealed Islam, we left Al-Rabdah, with a lady of ours with us, until we camped near the The city. While we were sitting, a man wearing two garments came to us and greeted us and said: Where are the people from? So we said: From Al-Rabdha, and we had a red camel. He said: Will you sell me this camel? We said: Yes, and he said: How much? So we said: With such-and-such, a saa’ of dates. He said: I took it. He did not investigate, so he took the camel’s snout and carried it until it hid in the walls. The city, and we said to one another: Do you know the man? But there was no one who knew him, so the people blamed one another and said: Do you give your camel to someone you do not know? Then the woman said: Do not blame me, for we have seen a man who does not deceive you. I have never seen anything more like the moon on a full night than his face. When it was Al-Ashi, a man came to us and said: May the peace, mercy, and blessings of God be upon you. Are you the ones who came from Al-Rabadha? We said: Yes. He said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to you, and he commands you to eat of these dates until you are satisfied. And eat yourselves until you have satisfied yourselves. So we ate of dates until we were satisfied, and we devoured them until you had satisfied yourselves. Then we came to Medina the next day, and behold, a Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing and addressing people on the pulpit, and I heard him say: “The hand of the Giver is on high. Begin with those you support: your mother and your father. And your sister, and your brother, and the lowest of you, the lowest of you.” Then a man from the Ansar said: O Messenger of God, these are Banu Tha’labah bin Yarubu’, who They killed so-and-so in pre-Islamic times, so take our revenge. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits and said: “No.” “A mother commits injustice against a child, a mother does not commit injustice against a child.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4219 - True"
"4220","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Thaqafi told me, Abu Kurayb told us, Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Uthman. Ibn Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present himself to people in a situation and say: “Is there a man He will carry me to his people, for the Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the words of my Lord.” He said: Then a man from Banu Hamadan came to him and said: I am. He said: Is it? Is there any protection among your people? He said: Yes, and asked him: “Where is he from?” He said: From Hamadan. Then the Hamadani man feared that his people would fear him, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Go to my people. So he informed them, then he met you a year ago. He said: “Yes.” So he set off and an Ansar delegation came in Rajab. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.” And they did not bring it out,” the last book of the Resurrection.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4220 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4221","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said, “I was sent to complete good morals.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4221 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4222","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Hisham, that he entered with Hakim ibn Aflah upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her. About her, he asked her and said: O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “Don’t you read the Qur’an? He said: Yes, she said: If the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, created the Qur’an, “this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4222 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4223","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Hamid bin Sahl Al-Thaghri told us, Arim bin Al-Fadl told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Ayyub, Muammar, and Al-Numan bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God did not curse May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, free from a curse mentioned, and he never struck anything with his hand unless he struck it in the path of God, and he was never asked about anything. So he prevented him, unless he was asked for a sin from which he was the furthest from people, and he never took revenge on himself for anything that was done to him, unless the sanctities of God were violated. So God will take revenge, and he is never given a choice between two matters except that he chooses the easier of the two. And if he made a covenant with Gabriel and studied it with him, he would be better. people with goodness from the blowing wind.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it in this context, and from the hadith of Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani. It is very strange, as Sulayman bin Harb and others narrated it on the authority of Hammad and they did not mention Ayyub, and Gharim is trustworthy and trustworthy.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4223 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4224","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “It is written in the Gospel that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not rude, nor harsh, nor vulgar.” in the markets, and does not repay the evil with the like, but rather pardons and forgives. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4224 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4225","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ja`far al-Adami, the reciter in Baghdad, told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Ibrahim al-Dawraqi told us, Ahmad bin Nasr bin Malik Al-Khuza’i, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Yahya bin Aqeel, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Abu Awfa said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to talk a lot, talk little, lengthen the prayer, shorten the sermon, and never “He refrains from walking with the servant and the widow until he has finished their needs.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4225 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4226","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, He said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Utbah, saying: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to mention a lot. He minimizes idle talk, lengthens the prayer, shortens the sermon, and does not refrain from walking with the servant and the widow until he has finished for them. “Their need.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “Al-Hakim said: “I presented these authentic hadiths as evidence of prophecy. Among the morals of our Master, the Chosen One, according to the words of God Almighty: {And We have chosen them with knowledge over the worlds} [Al-Dukhan: 32] and the saying of God Almighty: {Allah knows best where He will place His message} [Al-An'am: 124] And the Almighty says: {By the pen, and they do not write. You are not, by the grace of your Lord, mad, and indeed For you is a reward beyond gratitude, and indeed you are of a great creation} [Al-Qalam: 2] So listen to the correct verses after them.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4226 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4227","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, dictating, Harun bin Al-Abbas Al-Hashimi told us, Jandal bin Waqiq told us, Amr bin Aws Al-Ansari told us, Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “God revealed to Jesus that Peace be upon you, O Jesus. Believe in Muhammad and command those of your nation who meet him to believe in him. If it were not for Muhammad, I would not have created Adam, and if it were not for Muhammad, I would not have created Paradise. Nor fire. Indeed, I created the throne upon water, and it became disturbed, and I wrote upon it: “There is no god but God, and Muhammad is the Messenger of God,” and it remained at rest.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4227 - I think it was fabricated on Saeed"
"4228","Abu Saeed Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali told us, Abu Al-Harith told us Abdullah bin Muslim Al-Fihri, Ismail bin Maslamah told us, Abdul Rahman bin Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When Adam committed the sin, he said: O Lord, I ask you truly. Muhammad when you forgave me, so God said: O Adam, how did you know Muhammad when I did not create him? He said: O Lord, because when you created me with your hand and breathed into me of your Spirit, I raised my head and saw on the pillars of the throne written: There is no god but God. Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so I knew that you did not add anything to your name that made the creation more beloved to you. Then God said: You are right, O Adam. Indeed, he is the most beloved of creation to me. Call upon Me in His right, for I have forgiven you, and had it not been for Muhammad, I would not have created you.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is the first hadith I mentioned by Abd al-Rahman ibn Zaid bin Aslam in this book.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4228 - Rather, it is subject"
"4229","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Qarad Abu Nuh told us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Abu Musa, said: “Abu Talib went out to the Levant, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with him among sheikhs from Quraysh. When they saw the monk, they descended and shifted their saddlebags, so the monk came out to them. Before that, they were passing by him, but he did not come out to them or pay attention. He said: As they were dismounting, he began to pass through them until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: This is the Master of the Worlds. This is the Messenger of the Lord of the Worlds. God is sending him as a mercy to the worlds. The elders of Quraysh said to him: What do you know about that? He said: When you approached Aqaba, not a tree or a stone remained but it fell down in prostration, and you do not prostrate except to a prophet, and I recognize him by my ring. Prophethood, lower than the cartilage of his shoulder like an apple. Then he returned and prepared food for them, then came to them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Herding camels. He said: Send for him. He came, wearing a cloud over him. He said: Look at him. A cloud shades him. When he approached the people, he found them. They preceded him to the top of the tree, and when he was sitting, the top of the tree leaned on him, and he said: Look at the top of the tree. He leaned on it, while he was standing on it. He appealed to them not to take him to the Romans, because if the Romans saw him, they would recognize him by name and kill him. He turned around and saw that he was with seven people. They came from the Romans, so he met them and said: What brings you? They said: We have come, for this Prophet is leaving this month, and there is no path left without people being sent to it, and we have been sent to this path of his. So he said The monk asked them: Did you leave behind anyone better than you? They said: No. They said: We only told him his news, so we were sent to this path of yours. He said: Have you seen a matter that God wanted to accomplish? Can he? Did any of the people respond to him? They said: No, he said: So they pledged allegiance to him, so they pledged allegiance to him and stayed with him. He said: Then the monk came to them and said: I ask you by God, which of you is his guardian? Abu Talib said: He continued to appeal to him until he responded and Abu Bakr sent Bilal with him, and the monk provided him with cakes and oil. “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4229 - I think it is fabricated, so some of it is false"
"4230","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Haywa bin Shurayh Al-Hadrami told us, Baqiyah bin Al-Walid told us, Buhair bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Utbah bin Abd al-Sulami, that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how What was the beginning of your business, O Messenger of God? He said: “My caregiver was one of the Banu Sa’d bin Bakr, so I and a son of hers set off with us, and we did not take any provisions with us, so I said: O my brother.” Go, and bring us some provisions from our mother. So my brother set off, and I was with the camel, and two white birds arrived as if they were eagles, and he said: One of them to its owner: Is it him? He said: Yes, so they came quickly and took me and flattened me to the back and split my stomach, then they took out my heart, split it open and took out two clots from it. They were black, and one of them said to his companion: “His portion,” meaning, write it down and seal it with the seal of the Prophet. So one of them said to its companion, “Put it on a cuff.” And put a thousand of his female slaves on a scale. When I looked at the thousand above me, I had pity that they would fall down on me. They said: If only his female slaves had been weighed against him. He turned toward them, then they departed and left me, and I was greatly dispersed. Then I went to my mother and told her what I had seen, and she was afraid that he had been confused. With me, she said, “I seek refuge in God.” So she set off her camel and put me on the mount, and she rode behind me until we reached my mother, and she said, “I have fulfilled my trust and my pledge.” I told her about what I had met, but that did not frighten her. She said: I saw a light emanating from me that illuminated the palaces of the Levant. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that A Muslim, and they did not produce it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4230 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4231","Abu Abbas Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Madani told us in Bukhara, Abdullah bin Mahmoud told us, Abdan bin Sayyar told us, Ahmad bin Abd told us Allah Al-Barqi, Yazid bin Yazid Al-Balawi told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and we stayed at a certain place, when a man was in the valley saying: O God, make me one of the people of the nation.” Muhammad, the late and forgiven, the one who will be rewarded, said: So I looked at the valley and saw a man whose height was more than three hundred cubits, and he said to me: Who are you? He said: I said: Anas bin Malik, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Where is he? I said: He is the one who hears what you say. He said: Then go to him and convey my greetings to him, and say to him: Your brother Elias conveys my greetings to you. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I informed him, so he came and met him, so he embraced him and greeted him. Then they sat talking, and he said to him: O Messenger of God, I am only eating in... Every year there is a day, and this is the day of my breaking the fast, so you and I eat. Then a table descended to them from heaven containing bread, fish, and celery, and they ate. He fed me and we prayed the afternoon prayer, then he bid him farewell, then I saw him passing on the clouds towards the sky. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4231 - Rather, it is a matter of God’s ugliness in his situation"
"4232","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, On the authority of Ali bin Murrah, on the authority of his father, he said: I traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw something wondrous in him. We went down to a certain place and he said: “ Go to these two trees and say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tells you to get together. So I went and said this to them: So each one of them was torn from its roots, and each one passed to its companion. They all met together, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided. Then he said: “Go and tell them, so that each one of them may return to her place.” So I came to them and said that to them, so each one returned. One woman went to her place and a woman came to him and said: This son of mine has had a disease for seven years that has taken him twice a day, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bring him closer.” She brought him closer to him, and he spit in his mouth and said: “Come out, the enemy of God. I am the Messenger of God.” Then the Messenger of God said to her. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When we return, let us know what he has done.” When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned, she received him and two rams with her. And the fat and the fat, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Take this ram and take from it whatever you want.” She said: By the One who honored you, what We saw something of him since we parted. Then a camel came to him and stood in front of him. He saw that his eyes were tearing up, so he sent to his companions and said: “What is the matter with your camel?” Is this your complaint? They said: We were working on him, but when he grew up and his work went away, we agreed to slaughter him tomorrow, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not slaughter him.” “And put it among the camels to be with them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4232 - True"
"4233","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Al-Nu’man told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard my father He narrates, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, that he told him that “a gathering was with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he made the people eat from it. Whenever one people were full, other people would sit in their place. He also said the same thing until the first prayer. He said: Man: It supplies something? So Samurah said: “It was not extended except from the sky.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4233 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4234","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Lakhmi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Al-Muttalib told me Ibn Abdullah Ibn Hantab Al-Makhzoumi, he said: Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Amra Al-Ansari told me, my father told me, he said: We were with the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during a campaign, and the people were afflicted with starvation, so the people asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to slaughter some of their backs. They said: God will inform us of them. When Omar ibn al-Khattab saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was about to give them permission to slaughter each other. their backs and said: O Messenger of God, how will we be if we meet the enemy tomorrow hungry in men? But if you decide, O Messenger of God, to call the people With the remains of their provisions, the people began to bring handfuls of food, and on top of that, the highest among them was the one who brought a handful of dates and gathered them, “Then He stood up and called for what God wished for him to call, then he called the army with their containers, then he ordered them to mobilize what was left of the army, but they left nothing but a container. They filled it, and something like it remained. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until his molars became visible, and he said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” “And I bear witness that I am the Messenger of God. No servant of God who believes in it will meet God except that he will be shielded from the Fire.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4234 - True"
"4235","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani informed us of Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghifari informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Usama ibn Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of a ship, he said: I sailed the sea in a ship and it broke, so I mounted a plank from it and it threw me into a thicket. There was a lion there, and he did not care for me except with it. I said: “O Abu Al-Harith, I am the freedman of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He lowered his head and winked. With his shoulder, he was wretched, and he kept winking at me and guiding me to the path until he set me on the road. When he put me on the road, he was worried, so I thought he was bidding me farewell. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4235 - True"
"4236","Abu Muhammad Al-Hasan bin Ibrahim Al-Aslami Al-Farsi narrated to me from the origin of his book, Ja’far bin Darastawayh narrated to us, Al-Yaman bin Saeed narrated to us. Al-Masisi, Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Masry told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: We were sitting around the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a local Bedouin Yemeni Arab entered, riding a red camel, and shouted at the door. The mosque, so he entered and said the salutations, then sat down. When he had died, they said: O Messenger of God, the she-camel under the Bedouin was theft. He said: “It is a sin.” Clear evidence? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “O Ali, take what God owes you from a Bedouin if proof is established against him, and if it is not established, return him to me.” He said: So the Bedouin knocked for an hour, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Arise, O Bedouin, for the command of God, or else present your argument.” So the she-camel from Behind the door: By the One who sent you with honor, O Messenger of God, this man did not steal from me, and no one has taken possession of me except him. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Oh Bedouin, what did you say to the one who said it with your excuse?” He said: I said: Oh God, you are not a Lord. We have narrated to You, nor is there a god with You who has helped You in our creation, nor is there a Lord with You, so we doubt your Lordship. You are our Lord. As we say, and beyond what those who say, I ask you to bless Muhammad and to acquit me of my innocence. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “By the One who sent me with dignity, O Bedouins, I have seen the angels approaching the mouths of the alleys writing your statement, so increase your blessings upon me.” The narrators of this hadith on the authority of the last of them are trustworthy, and this I do not know of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Masry.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4236 - It is a lie"
"4237","Abu Bakr Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How do I know that you are the Messenger of God? He said: “Do you think that if I call this stalk of this palm tree, will you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?” He said: Yes, he said: So he called the stalk and made the stalk descend from the palm tree until it fell to the ground and began to jump until he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then he said to him: “Go back.” He went back until he returned to his place. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4237 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4238","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzaki told us, Yusuf bin Musa Al-Marwazi told us, Abbad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Walid bin Abi Thawr told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mecca, and he went out for some And no tree or mountain faced him without saying: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4238 - True"
"4239","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi told us, Abd al-Malik ibn Kamil al-Raqqashi told us, Wahb ibn Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, he said: I fell ill and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came upon me, and I said, Oh God, if it is my time He has come, so comfort me, and if He is late, raise me up, and if there is calamity, then be patient with me. He said: “What did you say?” So I returned, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, heal him, O God, grant him health.” Then he said: “Arise,” so I got up, and that pain did not return to me. After that, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4239 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4240","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Daqqaq told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Ya’qub bin Ishaq told us Al-Hadrami, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, Abu Kathir Al-Anazi told us, he said: Abu Hurairah said: There is not a male or female believer on the face of the earth. Except that He loves me. He said: I said: What do you know about that, O Abu Hurairah? He said: I used to invite my mother to Islam but she refused, and one day I invited her and she made me hear about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I was inviting my mother to Islam but she refused me and I I called her one day, and she told me about you something that I dislike. So pray to God, O Messenger of God, to guide Abu Hurairah’s mother to Islam. So they prayed for her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I returned to my mother to give her the good news of the invitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When I was at the door, the door It was closed, so I knocked on the door and heard Hassi, so she put on her clothes and put her veil on her head and said: Be gentle, O Abu Hurairah, so she opened for me. The door, and when I entered, she said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so I returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I I cry from joy, just as I used to cry from sadness, and I started saying, “Preach good news, O Messenger of God. God has answered your call and God has guided my father’s mother.” Kitten to Islam, so I said: I pray to God to make me and my mother beloved to His faithful servants and to make them beloved to us. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said God, upon him be peace, said: “O God, make this servant of Yours, and his mother, beloved to Your faithful servants, and make them beloved to them.” There is not a believer on earth, nor “I am a believer unless he loves me and I love him.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4240 - True"
"4241","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Sulaiman Al-Burlusi told us, Dirar bin Surad told us, Aidh bin Habib told us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them both, he said: So-and-so was sitting next to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spoke about something, his face would shine. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Be like that.” He did not. He continued to tremble until he died. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4241 - Dirar bin Sard is weak"
"4242","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Dawud bin Suleiman Al-Zahid told me, Abu Ali Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Ash’ath Al-Kufi told me in Egypt, Abu Al-Hasan told me Musa bin Ismail bin Musa bin Ja’far bin Muhammad, my father told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of his father, Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that he was a Jew, and he was called Juraijra. He had authority over the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he received dinars, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid money and said to him: “O Jew, I do not have anything to give you.” He said: I will not separate from you, O Muhammad, until You give me, so he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Then I will sit with you.” So he sat with him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in that place during the afternoon prayer. And the afternoon, and the sunset, and the afterlife, and the afterlife, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were threatening him and threatening him, but he became wise The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “What are you doing with it?” They said: O Messenger of God, a Jew is imprisoning you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My Lord has forbidden me from being unjust to a covenanter or anyone else.” When The day departed, and the Jew said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and he said: Half of my wealth is for the sake of God. By God, I did not do what I did to you except to look at your description in the Torah: Muhammad bin Abdullah, born in Mecca, and emigrants. In Thebes, and his rule in the Levant is neither rude nor harsh, nor does he make noise in the markets, nor is he adorned with obscenity, nor does he speak treacherously. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and you are the Messenger of God. This is my money, so judge it according to what God has shown you. The Jew had a lot of money.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4242 - A completely objectionable hadith"
"4243","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yahya bin Ma’in told us, Uqba Al-Mujaddar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The Quraysh continued to be united until Abu Talib died.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”"
"4244","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: “The name of Al-Najashi was Mashama, which in Arabic is Atiya, but Negus is the name of the king, as you say about Chosroes and Heraclius. Ibn Ishaq said: This is a letter from the Prophet. Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to the Negus: “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is the letter of Muhammad, the Messenger of God, to the Negus, the great Abyssinian.” Peace be upon the one who follows guidance, believes in God and His Messenger, and bears witness that there is no god but God alone, who has no partner, who does not take a companion or son, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, I invite you with the supplication of God, for I am the Messenger of God, so submit. {O People of the Book, come to A common word between us and you: that we worship none but Allah, and do not associate anything with Him, and do not take some of us as lords besides Allah.} [Al Imran: 64] The verse, and if you refuse, then upon you is the sin of the Christians. “Muhammad bin Ishaq al-Qurashi, named after the Negus, was not followed up on the fact that he is a Muslim. The authentic reports are It is mentioned in the two authentic books as the alif and the letter referred to it in the book of the Messenger of God.”"
"4245","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Khaled bin Yazid Al-Qurashi told us, Khadij bin Muawiyah, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him He handed over to the Negus, while we were about eighty men, and he mentioned the hadith in its length, as I narrated it in the interpretation: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” They did not publish it, and let the seeker of knowledge know that it was Al-Najashi who published it before the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote about it. The evidence for that is their narration in the two Sahih books on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Salamah and Umm Habibah mentioned A church and that there are images in the land of Abyssinia, the Hadith."
"4246","Ismail bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told me, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told me, Muhammad bin Falih told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab: “Uthman bin Affan and his wife Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left as immigrants from Mecca. To Abyssinia, then they went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Mecca, then they migrated to Medina. The two sheikhs agreed to bring The hadith of Ibn Abi Shaybah and others on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Adi, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, on the narration of Uthman ibn Affan went to the land of Abyssinia and narrated the hadith in its entirety, so I summarized it on the narration of Musa bin Uqba on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, and he mentioned in The significance is that Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as they mentioned, was not seen among the Arabs or the Ethiopians more beautiful than her.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4246 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4247","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abu He asked for verses from the Negus exhorting them to be good neighbors and defend them: “\n [Long Sea]\n So that people may know that Muhammad is... a minister of Moses and the Messiah, the son of Mary.\n He brought us guidance just like what they brought with him... so each one guides and protects by the command of God.\n And you recite it in your book... with the truth of the hadith, not the hadith of the astrologist.\n And no group of them comes to you... by your grace, but they return with honor.”"
"4248","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Ishaq bin Saeed Al-Umawi Al-Saeedi told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Umm Khaled, bint Khalid, she said: I came from the land of Abyssinia and I am a Juwayriyah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, clothed me with a garment for her. Notable figures, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, began wiping the notables with his hand and saying: “Sanah, Sunnah” - meaning: good, good - “This is an authentic hadith based on The conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not include it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4248 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4249","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Al-Haytham bin Khalid told us, Abu Ghassan Al-Nahdi told us, Al-Ajlah bin Abd told us God, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: When Ja’far bin Abi Talib came from the land of Abyssinia, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “I do not know which of the two I should be happy with, the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Ja’far.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4249 - True"
"4250","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Saeed bin Yahya bin Saeed Al-Umawi told us, my father told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq, Yazid bin Abi Habib told us, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghasila al-Sanabihi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: “There were eleven of us at the first Aqaba of the following year, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to us with the pledge of allegiance of women.” “Before he imposed war on us.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4250 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"4251","Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Muqri told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Adni told me, Yahya told us Bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stayed for ten years. He follows the people to their homes during the season, and to Majnah and Ukaz and to their homes from Mina. “Whoever gives me shelter, whoever supports me, until I convey the messages of my Lord, to him Paradise? He did not find anyone to support him or shelter him, until the man left Egypt or Yemen to his relatives, and his people came to him and said: To him: Beware of the boy of Quraysh, lest he tempt you, and he walks among their camps, calling them to God Almighty, pointing at him with the fingers, until God sent us from Yathrib, and a man from among us comes to him and believes in him, and recites to him the Qur’an, and he returns to his family and they accept his Islam, until there is no longer any There is not one of the houses of the Ansar except that there is in it a group of Muslims, who profess Islam, and God sent us to him, so we took a decision and gathered together and said: Until the time when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is chased into the mountains of Mecca and becomes afraid,So we traveled until we came to him during the season, and we agreed on the Pledge of Aqaba, and his uncle Abbas said to him: O son of my brother, I do not know who these people are. Those who came to you: I am acquainted with the people of Yathrib, so we gathered with him, one and two men. When al-Abbas looked at our faces, he said: These are A people we do not know, these are young people, so we said: O Messenger of God, for what do we pledge allegiance to you? He said: “You pledge allegiance to me for listening and obedience in times of activity and laziness, and for spending during hardship and ease, and for enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong.” evil, and that you say about God, “Do not let the blame of a blamer overtake you,” and that you support me when I come against you, and that you prevent me from what you prevent me from. Yourselves, your wives, and your children, and for you is Paradise.” So we stood up and pledged allegiance to him, and As’ad ibn Zurarah took by the hand, and he was the youngest of seventy except That he said: Slowly, O people of Yathrib, we did not strike the livers of the camels at him unless we knew that he was the Messenger of God and that his departure Today is the separation of all the Arabs and the killing of your best, and the sword will bite you. Either you are a people who will be patient with it when it touches you and with the killing Your choice and separating from all the Arabs, so take it and your reward is with God, or you are afraid of yourselves, so leave it, for it is an excuse when... God Almighty,They said: O Asaad, extend your hand from us, for by God we will neither abandon this pledge of allegiance nor resign from it. He said: So we rose up to him, man by man, and he attacked us. That He may give us Paradise with that. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration that includes the Pledge of Aqaba, but they did not exclude it.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4251 - True"
"4252","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Yahya bin Bukayr told us, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: “There were three months, or close to it, between the night of Aqaba and the migration of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the pledge of allegiance to the Ansar was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him on the night of Aqaba in Dhul-Hijjah, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Medina in the month of Rabi’ al-Awwal.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4252 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4253","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Uqabi told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Qubaisah bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, And others, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the captains of Al-Ansar: “Do you shelter me or protect me?” They said: Yes, so what do we have? He said: “Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4253 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"4254","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Shairi told us, Muhammad bin Issam told us, Hafs bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, that he said: “The first of the immigrants to come to Medina was Mus’ab bin Umair and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they were reciting to us, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and I had recited Praise the Name of Your Most High Lord and a surah from Al-Mufassil, then Saad bin Malik and Ammar bin Yasser came, then Omar bin Al-Khattab came in the twenty, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and what We were happy with something and we were happy with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It caused the women and children to run and say: This is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4254 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4255","Abu Al-Nasr Ahmad bin Al-Fadl, the writer of Hamdan, informed us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us Al-Khuzami, Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: I said to Urwah bin Al-Zubayr: How long did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stay in Mecca? He said: Ten years. I said: Ibn Abbas says: “He stayed for some ten years.” He said: He only took it from the poet’s saying. Sufyan bin Uyaynah: Yahya bin Saeed told us that he said: I heard an old woman from the Ansar saying: I saw Ibn Abbas going to Sarmat bin Qais to learn from him. These verses:\n [Long Sea]\n\n He stayed with the Quraysh for a few ten days... he remembers if he met a loyal friend.\n He presented himself among the people of the seasons... and he did not see anyone to provide shelter, nor did he see an inviter.\n When he came to us and the seeds settled in him... and he became pleased with his goodness and satisfied.\n And what he feared was darkness, an oppressor... and he became distant, and what he feared was a transgressor from people.\n We gave him money out of our wealth... and our lives in times of persecution and misfortune.\n We are hostile to the one who is hostile to all people... justly, even if he is a beloved and beloved one.\n And we know that there is nothing besides Him... and that the Book of God has become a guide.”\n This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it is the first thing on which the argument can be made regarding the status of our Master the Chosen One, may God bless him. He lived in Mecca for a period of ten years, and he has a valid witness according to the condition of a Muslim.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4255 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"4256","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ammar Ibn Abi Ammar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, resided in Mecca for fifteen years, seven and eight He saw the light and heard the sound, and he stayed in the city for ten days.”\n [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 4256 - According to Muslim’s condition"
